  { "id": "sin75", "front": "(HL) Exact value of $\\sin75^\\circ$.", "back": "$\\sin(45^\\circ + 30^\\circ) = \\frac{\\sqrt2}2\\cdot\\frac{\\sqrt3}2 + \\frac{\\sqrt2}2\\cdot\\frac12 = \\dfrac{\\sqrt6 + \\sqrt2}4$.", "concept": "Compound angles", "kind": "application" },
  { "id": "tan-pi12", "front": "(HL) Exact value of $\\tan\\frac\\pi{12}$.", "back": "$\\tan\\left(\\frac\\pi3 - \\frac\\pi4\\right) = \\dfrac{\\sqrt3 - 1}{1 + \\sqrt3} = 2 - \\sqrt3$.", "concept": "Compound angles", "kind": "application" },
  { "id": "sin-ab-example", "front": "(HL) $\\sin A = \\frac35$, $\\cos B = \\frac5{13}$, both acute. Find $\\sin(A + B)$.", "back": "$\\cos A = \\frac45$, $\\sin B = \\frac{12}{13}$: $\\frac35\\cdot\\frac5{13} + \\frac45\\cdot\\frac{12}{13} = \\frac{63}{65}$.", "concept": "Compound angles", "kind": "application" },
  { "id": "double-from-compound", "front": "(HL) How do the double angle formulae follow from compound angles?", "back": "Put $B = A$: $\\sin2A = 2\\sin A\\cos A$, $\\cos2A = \\cos^2A - \\sin^2A$, $\\tan2A = \\dfrac{2\\tan A}{1 - \\tan^2A}$.", "concept": "Double angle (tan)", "kind": "derivation" },
  { "id": "expand-example", "front": "(HL) Expand $\\sin\\left(x + \\frac\\pi3\\right)$.", "back": "$\\frac12\\sin x + \\frac{\\sqrt3}2\\cos x$.", "concept": "Compound angles", "kind": "application" },
  { "id": "sum-identity-proof", "front": "(HL) Show $\\sin(A + B) + \\sin(A - B) \\equiv 2\\sin A\\cos B$.", "back": "Expand both: the $\\cos A\\sin B$ terms cancel, leaving $2\\sin A\\cos B$.", "concept": "Compound angles", "kind": "application" },
  { "id": "tan2-condition", "front": "(HL) When is $\\tan2\\theta = \\dfrac{2\\tan\\theta}{1 - \\tan^2\\theta}$ undefined?", "back": "When $\\tan\\theta = \\pm1$ (then $2\\theta$ is an odd multiple of $\\frac\\pi2$) or when $\\tan\\theta$ itself is undefined.", "concept": "Double angle (tan)", "kind": "condition" },
